{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"ExponentialBackoff","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExponentialBackoff.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff.swift#L26"},"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How long "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" waits before each new attempt at a batch that wasn’t delivered:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary exponential backoff, each nominal wait twice the one before, up to a maximum, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"jitter."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SQ","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SH","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts","title":"Waiting between attempts"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(initialDelay:maximumDelay:jitter:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/init(jitter:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/initialDelay","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/jitter-swift.property","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/maximumDelay"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum"],"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExponentialBackoff","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExponentialBackoff()"},{"type":"text","text":" has nominal waits of 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 32 seconds, then 60 seconds for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every retry after that, with full jitter, as this one does:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let backoff = try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(1), maximumDelay: .seconds(60), jitter: .full)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the nominal wait. What "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" sleeps before each retry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depends on the backoff’s jitter:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/full","type":"reference"},{"text":", the default: a random wait, at least zero and less than the nominal one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawn afresh before each retry from the destination’s random number generator.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": the nominal wait. It is exact when both delays count their attoseconds in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"53 significant bits or fewer, as any whole number of milliseconds under 295 seconds does;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise it is within about one part in 2⁵³ of it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Jitter is on by default because apps tend to be refused all at once. A rate limiter’s window,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or an outage ending, refuses many apps at the same moment. Without jitter they would all retry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the same moments too, and each wave would be refused like the one before. Full jitter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spreads each wave over the whole wait. It also halves the average wait, so an app retries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"about twice as often during a long outage."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/SH":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SH","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Hashable"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/Jitter-swift.enum/none":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"none","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The nominal wait, exactly."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/jitter-swift.enum\/none","title":"ExponentialBackoff.Jitter.none"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/Equatable-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"kind":"article","title":"Equatable Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Equatable-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/exponentialbackoff\/equatable-implementations","role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/Jitter-swift.enum/full":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"full","kind":"ident